# TODO — features/project

- Open in Editor for Uploads lands on the "not available yet" placeholder
  (Scratch opens in the Editor). Tracked in https://github.com/haowjy/meridian-flow/issues/625.
- The dock document slot is synced by an effect (`dock/dock-view-store.ts`
  `syncDocumentScope`, called from the `ProjectView.tsx` layout effect). Derive
  the shown document from the route's Work instead of syncing it. Deferred to a
  dedicated side-panel work item (mention-first peeking, #625), which also
  decides whether returning to a Work reopens its document.
- Focus rings after programmatic focus: a screen heading focused on navigation
  (e.g. the Work list's "Work" h1) shows its ring, and the Archived tab keeps its
  ring after a refused Archive returns the Work to Active
  (`work/useArchiveFocusFollow.ts`). Programmatic focus should not paint a
  keyboard ring, and focus-follow should return with the Work on refusal.
- Composer attachments still ride on Work-scoped `uploads://`
  (`components/app/composer/Composer.tsx` `ComposerUploadPort` →
  `client/api/upload-intake-api.ts` → the Work upload route), though the Work
  page no longer shows Uploads. Rescope them to the thread lineage and delete
  the Work `uploads://` scheme:
  [#631](https://github.com/haowjy/meridian-flow/issues/631). Uploading into
  the file tree is [#630](https://github.com/haowjy/meridian-flow/issues/630).
- Reloading a document's old address steps through its earlier names before
  settling: the removal coordinator replays the move history one repair at a
  time. Bounded and pre-existing; repair straight to the current locator.
- The phone document header has no Apply or Discard during review
  (`mobile/MobileDocumentHost.tsx`); the writer reaches them through Open chat.
  Give the phone review the header's dispositions.
- The phone document host has no recovery for a failed live open:
  `mobile/MobileDocumentHost.tsx` calls `useLiveDocumentBinding` but never uses
  its `retry`, and it does not retry when the resource availability revision
  advances the way the desktop `ContextTabSessionBoundary` does. Give the phone
  host the same Retry and revision retry. Found in knowledge capture for
  draft-review-repair.
